  "notes": [
    {
      "note": "Arms simulate layer-2 access scheduling over the real table\u0027s row addressing with a synthetic token stream; production qwen4exp forward integration is not implemented and no claim here covers it."
    },
    {
      "note": "The stream uses zipf token ids (a cubed-uniform skew over a 262144-id vocabulary window concentrates row frequencies so hot-slot selection has something to select) with EOS cut and missing-predecessor windows mixed in; policy comparisons hold this stream identical across arms."
    },
    {
      "note": "hot-resident-prefetch versus hot-resident-no-prefetch isolates what staying resident buys from what prefetch overlap buys; demand-only is the floor of both."
    }
  ]
